{"text": "PRR42ZTO\n\nKarina Casas\n\nFrom: Rasic, Peter <prasic@elmontepd.org>\nSent: Monday, July 01, 2019 2:55 PM\nTo: City Clerk\nCec: Knight, Douglas; Chao, Jason\nSubject: FW: California Public Records Act Request: Amazon/Ring Records from El Monte\nAttachments: image001.png\n\nPRA received at the Watch Commander\u2019s email on 7/1/2019 at around 1430 hours.\n\nEL MONTE\nPete Rasic, Lieutenant - El Monte Police Department\n11333 Valley Blvd., El Monte, Ca., 91731\n\nprasic@elmontepd.org\n(626) 580-2100\n\nFrom: 76404-68567905@requests.muckrock.com [mailto:76404-68567905@requests.muckrock.com]\nSent: Monday, July 01, 2019 2:32 PM\nTo: Watch Commanders\n\nSubject: California Public Records Act Request: Amazon/Ring Records from El Monte Ss =\nre\n. t BR\nEl Monte Police Department ~ Rs\nPRA Office Uv 3s a\n11333 Valley Boulevard w =\nEl Monte, CA 91731 on 5\nw\nJuly 1, 2019\nTo Whom It May Concern:\n\nPursuant to the California Public Records Act, I hereby request the following records:\n\nAny emails, written communications, documents, or other communications between officials from the El Monte\nPolice Department and representatives of the corporations \"Amazon\" and/or \"Ring.\"\n\nWe seek El Monte Police Department records of any kind, including electronic records, audiotapes, videotapes,\nand photographs, as well as letters, emails, facsimiles, telephone messages, voice mail messages and transcripts,\nnotes, and minutes of any meetings. The search should be limited to responsive records created between January\n1, 2018 and the day the request is fulfilled.\n\nOur request includes any attachments to these records. No category of material should be omitted from search,\ncollection, and production. You may not exclude searches of files or emails in the personal custody of your\nofficials, such as personal email accounts.",
